  "verbalization": "Arformoterol is shown to bind to Cyp2a6 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the same functional pathway, where they catalyze the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid, a process that generates bioactive lipid mediators. The shared involvement of Cyp2a6 and Cyp2d6 in this pathway suggests that Arformoterol may influence the activity of Cyp2c9, which is also part of this metabolic process. The evidence from the three paths indicates a potential mechanism by which Arformoterol could modulate Cyp2c9 activity, likely through the inhibition of arachidonic acid metabolism. The consistent scores across the paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible relationship, supported by the shared functional roles of the enzymes involved. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a common pathway, and the evidence is consistent across different binding sites and enzyme activities.",
